{"id":159,"date":"2026-07-09T14:30:49","date_gmt":"2026-07-09T14:30:49","guid":{"rendered":"http:\/\/localhost:8181\/between-tenants-the-turnover-hvac-routine-for-shippensburg-duplexes\/"},"modified":"2026-07-14T19:43:55","modified_gmt":"2026-07-14T19:43:55","slug":"between-tenants-the-turnover-hvac-routine-for-shippensburg-duplexes","status":"publish","type":"page","link":"http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/between-tenants-the-turnover-hvac-routine-for-shippensburg-duplexes\/","title":{"rendered":"The Thermostat War in Shippensburg Duplexes Has No Winner"},"content":{"rendered":"\n<div class=\"wp-block-cover alignfull s-hero-offset\" style=\"min-height:500px;padding-top:6rem;padding-right:3rem;padding-bottom:6rem;padding-left:3rem;aspect-ratio:unset;\"><span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-cover__background has-contrast-background-color has-background-dim-40 has-background-dim\"><\/span><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"1024\" height=\"1024\" class=\"wp-block-cover__image-background wp-image-1761\" alt=\"thermostat - professional HVAC service photo\" src=\"\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez2-thermostat-1.png\" srcset=\"http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez2-thermostat-1.png 1024w, http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez2-thermostat-1-300x300.png 300w, http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez2-thermostat-1-150x150.png 150w, http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez2-thermostat-1-768x768.png 768w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px\" \/><div class=\"wp-block-cover__inner-container has-global-padding is-layout-constrained wp-container-core-cover-is-layout-15083543 wp-block-cover-is-layout-constrained\">\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group s-hero-offset__card has-global-padding is-layout-constrained wp-container-core-group-is-layout-b267b866 wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained\" style=\"padding-top:3rem;padding-right:3rem;padding-bottom:3rem;padding-left:3rem\">\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Thermostat wars end here<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">The thermostat war between landlords and tenants in college duplexes has generated more text messages than actual thermal comfort.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-buttons is-content-justification-center is-layout-flex wp-container-core-buttons-is-layout-35f06ea7 wp-block-buttons-is-layout-flex\">\n<div class=\"wp-block-button\"><a class=\"wp-block-button__link wp-element-button\" href=\"\/contact\/\">Schedule the Walkthrough<\/a><\/div>\n<\/div>\n<\/div>\n\n<\/div><\/div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"s-trust-bar\"><div class=\"s-trust__item\">15+ Years Serving PA<\/div><div class=\"s-trust__item\">Licensed &amp; Insured<\/div><div class=\"s-trust__item\">Same-Day Emergency<\/div><div class=\"s-trust__item\">Local to Your Area<\/div><\/div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group has-global-padding is-layout-constrained wp-container-core-group-is-layout-633910b2 wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained\" style=\"padding-top:4.5rem;padding-right:2.5rem;padding-bottom:4.5rem;padding-left:2.5rem\">\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Why Rental Duplexes Defeat HVAC Systems<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Student housing economics create a structural conflict between those who pay utility bills and those who experience indoor temperature. Property owners who cover heat and electricity as part of all-inclusive rent watch winter utility costs spiral when tenants treat thermostats as binary switches\u2014either full heat or completely off. Renters who pay separately receive angry landlord messages about settings they cannot remember changing.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">The underlying problem is rarely the thermostat itself but poorly insulated duplex construction, heating systems sized without considering separate metering, and the absence of smart controls that could bridge financial responsibility and comfort preferences. This town&#039;s rental housing stock skews toward converted single-family homes and purpose-built duplexes from the 1970s and 1980s, when insulation codes were minimal.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">The typical Shippensburg rental duplex started as a single-family home either split vertically or with an upstairs apartment added when university enrollment expanded. The original heating system\u2014often a single furnace with ductwork designed for one household\u2014now serves two separate living spaces with different occupancy patterns and thermostat preferences.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">The conversion work rarely included proper insulation in newly created demising walls, so thermal transfer between units means one tenant&#039;s heating choices directly impact the other&#039;s comfort and costs.<\/p>\n\n<\/div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group alignfull s-band s-band--sand has-tint-background-color has-background has-global-padding is-layout-constrained wp-container-core-group-is-layout-08713647 wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained\" style=\"padding-top:6rem;padding-right:2.5rem;padding-bottom:6rem;padding-left:2.5rem\">\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group has-global-padding is-layout-constrained wp-container-core-group-is-layout-633910b2 wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained\" style=\"padding-top:4.5rem;padding-right:2.5rem;padding-bottom:4.5rem;padding-left:2.5rem\">\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-element-heading has-text-align-center wp-block-heading\">Thermal Management in Student Housing<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group s-table s-table--modern has-global-padding is-layout-constrained wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained\">\n<figure class=\"wp-block-table\"><table class=\"has-fixed-layout\"><thead><tr><th>Challenge<\/th><th>Impact<\/th><th>Typical Cost to Fix<\/th><\/tr><\/thead><tbody><tr><td>Single furnace serving duplex<\/td><td>Unequal comfort, subsidy between units<\/td><td>$1,500\u2013$3,000<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>Original single-pane windows<\/td><td>Dramatic infiltration and radiant loss<\/td><td>$300\u2013$800 per zone<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>Inadequate attic insulation (R-19 or less)<\/td><td>40% of heating loss through ceiling<\/td><td>$1,200\u2013$2,200<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>Tenant-controlled thermostat abuse<\/td><td>20\u201330% utility overage during breaks<\/td><td>$200\u2013$400 smart control<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>No zoning or dampers<\/td><td>Impossible to balance comfort preferences<\/td><td>$1,800\u2013$3,500 retrofit<\/td><\/tr><\/tbody><\/table><\/figure>\n<\/div>\n\n<\/div>\n\n<\/div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group has-global-padding is-layout-constrained wp-container-core-group-is-layout-633910b2 wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained\" style=\"padding-top:4.5rem;padding-right:2.5rem;padding-bottom:4.5rem;padding-left:2.5rem\">\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-columns alignwide s-stats is-layout-flex wp-container-core-columns-is-layout-794e3cfa wp-block-columns-is-layout-flex\">\n<div class=\"wp-block-column s-stats__item is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow\">\n<p class=\"s-stats__number has-x-large-font-size wp-block-paragraph\">7<\/p>\n\n<p class=\"s-stats__label wp-block-paragraph\">Months heating season runs (Oct\u2013Apr)<\/p>\n<\/div>\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-column s-stats__item is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow\">\n<p class=\"s-stats__number has-x-large-font-size wp-block-paragraph\">15\u201330%<\/p>\n\n<p class=\"s-stats__label wp-block-paragraph\">Typical utility waste from mismanaged thermostats<\/p>\n<\/div>\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-column s-stats__item is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow\">\n<p class=\"s-stats__number has-x-large-font-size wp-block-paragraph\">$2,400+<\/p>\n\n<p class=\"s-stats__label wp-block-paragraph\">Average winter heating cost, poorly insulated duplex<\/p>\n<\/div>\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-column s-stats__item is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow\">\n<p class=\"s-stats__number has-x-large-font-size wp-block-paragraph\">2\u20133<\/p>\n\n<p class=\"s-stats__label wp-block-paragraph\">Tenant turnover cycles per year in student areas<\/p>\n<\/div>\n\n<\/div>\n\n<\/div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group has-global-padding is-layout-constrained wp-container-core-group-is-layout-633910b2 wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained\" style=\"padding-top:4.5rem;padding-right:2.5rem;padding-bottom:4.5rem;padding-left:2.5rem\">\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-media-text\" style=\"grid-template-columns:50% auto\"><figure class=\"wp-block-media-text__media\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"1024\" height=\"1024\" src=\"\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez2-thermostat-2.png\" alt=\"thermostat - professional HVAC service photo\" class=\"wp-image-1762\" srcset=\"http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez2-thermostat-2.png 1024w, http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez2-thermostat-2-300x300.png 300w, http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez2-thermostat-2-150x150.png 150w, http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez2-thermostat-2-768x768.png 768w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px\" \/><span class=\"s-img-badge s-img-badge--ai\" title=\"AI-generated (gemini-2.5-flash-image)\">AI<\/span><\/figure><div class=\"wp-block-media-text__content\">\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Smart Thermostats as Conflict Resolution<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Modern connected thermostats solve multiple problems simultaneously when deployed thoughtfully in rental properties. Remote access allows landlords to verify settings during vacancy without driving to the property. Usage tracking creates transparent records that resolve disputes about who set what temperature when. Geofencing can automatically implement setback temperatures when all occupants leave, saving energy without requiring tenants to remember manual adjustments.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Quality units cost under two hundred dollars installed, but psychological and legal barriers loom larger than financial ones. The optimal deployment model involves transparency and shared access rather than unilateral landlord control. Both tenants and property owners receive app access, with the system configured to send alerts when temperatures deviate from agreed ranges or when heating costs project to exceed budget targets.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">The lease includes specific language about acceptable temperature ranges, setback expectations during breaks, and procedures for resolving disagreements. This approach treats the thermostat as a communication tool that surfaces conflicts early rather than allowing resentment to build until someone receives an unexpected utility bill. Success requires treating installation as part of a larger conversation about expectations and responsibilities rather than as a surveillance tool.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">A landlord who secretly monitors settings without telling tenants violates the relationship and probably lease law. Tenants who deliberately override agreed-upon settings create the conflict the technology was meant to prevent. Both parties must understand what the system monitors, how data will be used, and what protections exist against abuse.<\/p>\n\n<\/div><\/div>\n\n<\/div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group has-global-padding is-layout-constrained wp-container-core-group-is-layout-633910b2 wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained\" style=\"padding-top:4.5rem;padding-right:2.5rem;padding-bottom:4.5rem;padding-left:2.5rem\">\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-media-text has-media-on-the-right\" style=\"grid-template-columns:auto 50%\"><div class=\"wp-block-media-text__content\">\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Zoning Solutions for Independent Control<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">True resolution of temperature disputes often requires physical system changes that allow independent climate control for spaces with different preferences and financial responsibilities. Retrofitting zoning into existing forced-air systems involves installing motorized dampers in ductwork that serve different areas, adding multiple thermostats, and sometimes upgrading control boards. For duplexes with separate utility meters per unit, proper zoning ensures each tenant pays only for their own heating choices.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">For properties where landlords cover utilities, zoning allows implementing maximum temperature limits for heat without making the building uniformly uncomfortable. The installation cost for basic two-zone or three-zone systems typically ranges from fifteen hundred to three thousand dollars depending on ductwork accessibility. That investment makes sense for properties that generate frequent tenant complaints, high utility costs, or turnover driven by comfort dissatisfaction.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Some Shippensburg landlords have discovered that advertising rental units with independent zone control and smart thermostats attracts more mature tenants willing to pay slightly higher rent for demonstrably better thermal management. This shifts the investment from cost to competitive advantage. Ductless mini-split heat pumps represent a simpler alternative for situations where full zoning is not financially feasible.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">These systems can be added to specific rooms that consistently experience comfort problems, providing supplemental heating and cooling that the occupant controls independently. They cost more initially than portable units but operate efficiently, include modern controls, and eliminate the safety objections landlords raise against space heaters.<\/p>\n\n<\/div><figure class=\"wp-block-media-text__media\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"1024\" height=\"768\" src=\"\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/3145968830_73d42a7d2e_b.jpg\" alt=\"attic insulation\" class=\"wp-image-189\" srcset=\"http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/3145968830_73d42a7d2e_b.jpg 1024w, http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/3145968830_73d42a7d2e_b-300x225.jpg 300w, http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/3145968830_73d42a7d2e_b-768x576.jpg 768w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px\" \/><span class=\"s-img-badge s-img-badge--stock\" title=\"&quot;The R11 attic insulation&quot; by zieak, BY, via Openverse\">Stock<\/span><\/figure><\/div>\n\n<\/div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group alignfull s-band s-band--sand has-tint-background-color has-background has-global-padding is-layout-constrained wp-container-core-group-is-layout-08713647 wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained\" style=\"padding-top:6rem;padding-right:2.5rem;padding-bottom:6rem;padding-left:2.5rem\">\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Services for Rental Property Owners<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-columns alignwide s-feature-row is-layout-flex wp-container-core-columns-is-layout-794e3cfa wp-block-columns-is-layout-flex\">\n<div class=\"wp-block-column s-card s-feature-card is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow\">\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-medium s-feature-card__img\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"1024\" height=\"683\" src=\"\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez-technician-2-1024x683.png\" alt=\"technician - professional HVAC service photo\" class=\"wp-image-1476\" srcset=\"http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez-technician-2-1024x683.png 1024w, http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez-technician-2-300x200.png 300w, http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez-technician-2-768x512.png 768w, http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez-technician-2.png 1536w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px\" \/><span class=\"s-img-badge s-img-badge--ai\" title=\"AI-generated (gpt-image-1)\">AI<\/span><\/figure>\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Smart Thermostat Installation<\/h3>\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Remote access, usage tracking, and geofencing controls with shared tenant app access and lockout capabilities.<\/p>\n<\/div>\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-column s-card s-feature-card is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow\">\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-medium s-feature-card__img\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"1024\" height=\"1024\" src=\"\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez2-technician-1.png\" alt=\"technician - professional HVAC service photo\" class=\"wp-image-1755\" srcset=\"http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez2-technician-1.png 1024w, http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez2-technician-1-300x300.png 300w, http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez2-technician-1-150x150.png 150w, http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez2-technician-1-768x768.png 768w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px\" \/><span class=\"s-img-badge s-img-badge--ai\" title=\"AI-generated (gemini-2.5-flash-image)\">AI<\/span><\/figure>\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Zoning System Retrofit<\/h3>\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Motorized dampers, multiple thermostats, and control upgrades to allow independent climate control per unit or room.<\/p>\n<\/div>\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-column s-card s-feature-card is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow\">\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-medium s-feature-card__img\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"1023\" height=\"575\" src=\"\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/9060093881_9c8364f29c_b.jpg\" alt=\"mini split heat pump\" class=\"wp-image-201\" srcset=\"http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/9060093881_9c8364f29c_b.jpg 1023w, http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/9060093881_9c8364f29c_b-300x169.jpg 300w, http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/9060093881_9c8364f29c_b-768x432.jpg 768w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 1023px) 100vw, 1023px\" \/><span class=\"s-img-badge s-img-badge--stock\" title=\"&quot;Back of house after Lennox Mini-split heat pump\/AC was installed into the Great Room.&quot; by Lani. Mar 13 1941 to Dec 13 2018. Rest in Peace, BY-ND, via Openverse\">Stock<\/span><\/figure>\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Mini-Split Heat Pump Add-Ons<\/h3>\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Ductless supplemental heating and cooling for problem zones or rooms where central system cannot satisfy comfort independently.<\/p>\n<\/div>\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-column s-card s-feature-card is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow\">\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-medium s-feature-card__img\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"1024\" height=\"1024\" src=\"\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez2-technician-2.png\" alt=\"technician - professional HVAC service photo\" class=\"wp-image-1756\" srcset=\"http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez2-technician-2.png 1024w, http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez2-technician-2-300x300.png 300w, http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez2-technician-2-150x150.png 150w, http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez2-technician-2-768x768.png 768w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px\" \/><span class=\"s-img-badge s-img-badge--ai\" title=\"AI-generated (gemini-2.5-flash-image)\">AI<\/span><\/figure>\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Pre-Lease HVAC Inspections<\/h3>\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Furnace testing, filter replacement, thermostat verification, condensate drain clearing, and emergency shutoff labeling before tenant move-in.<\/p>\n<\/div>\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-column s-card s-feature-card is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow\">\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-medium s-feature-card__img\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"1024\" height=\"768\" src=\"\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/51282276312_f3389b56f2_b.jpg\" alt=\"hvac technician repair\" class=\"wp-image-188\" srcset=\"http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/51282276312_f3389b56f2_b.jpg 1024w, http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/51282276312_f3389b56f2_b-300x225.jpg 300w, http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/51282276312_f3389b56f2_b-768x576.jpg 768w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px\" \/><span class=\"s-img-badge s-img-badge--stock\" title=\"&quot;AC Service&quot; by SuperTech HVAC Services, BY-SA, via Openverse\">Stock<\/span><\/figure>\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Envelope Improvements<\/h3>\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Attic insulation upgrades, air sealing, window weatherstripping, and basement rim joist insulation to reduce system stress.<\/p>\n<\/div>\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-column s-card s-feature-card is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow\">\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-medium s-feature-card__img\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"1024\" height=\"683\" src=\"\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez-technician-1-1024x683.png\" alt=\"technician - professional HVAC service photo\" class=\"wp-image-1475\" srcset=\"http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez-technician-1-1024x683.png 1024w, http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez-technician-1-300x200.png 300w, http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez-technician-1-768x512.png 768w, http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez-technician-1.png 1536w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px\" \/><span class=\"s-img-badge s-img-badge--ai\" title=\"AI-generated (gpt-image-1)\">AI<\/span><\/figure>\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Tenant Education &amp; Documentation<\/h3>\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Move-in guidance, system operation manuals, seasonal adjustment recommendations, and written procedures for comfort vs. cost decisions.<\/p>\n<\/div>\n\n<\/div>\n\n<\/div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group has-global-padding is-layout-constrained wp-container-core-group-is-layout-633910b2 wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained\" style=\"padding-top:4.5rem;padding-right:2.5rem;padding-bottom:4.5rem;padding-left:2.5rem\">\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Insulation and Air Sealing: Solving the Actual Problem<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group s-indent has-global-padding is-layout-constrained wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained\">\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Thermostat conflicts often distract from the fundamental issue that most Shippensburg rental duplexes are energy sieves that no HVAC system can heat efficiently. Addressing the building envelope returns more value per dollar spent than any equipment upgrade, but the work is unglamorous and invisible once complete. Landlords accustomed to thinking of HVAC as the heating system miss that walls, attic, and windows determine how well any heating system performs.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Priority improvements include: attic insulation upgrades to R-49 current code minimum; air sealing focused on attic access hatches, basement rim joists, and penetrations; window treatments or film reducing infiltration without replacement cost; proper weatherstripping on entry doors; and basement or crawlspace insulation preventing heat loss to ground. Each addresses specific leak sites that defeat any thermostat&#039;s ability to maintain consistent comfort.<\/p>\n<\/div>\n\n<\/div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group has-global-padding is-layout-constrained wp-container-core-group-is-layout-633910b2 wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained\" style=\"padding-top:4.5rem;padding-right:2.5rem;padding-bottom:4.5rem;padding-left:2.5rem\">\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list s-pills s-pills--ember\">\n<li>Smart controls prevent tenant-caused equipment damage<\/li>\n\n\n<li>Pre-lease inspections catch problems before emergencies<\/li>\n\n\n<li>7-month heating season requires October through April preparation<\/li>\n\n\n<li>Multi-zone ductless eliminates comfort complaints per room<\/li>\n\n\n<li>Rental turnover: inspect and document HVAC condition at each transition<\/li>\n\n<\/ul>\n\n<\/div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group has-global-padding is-layout-constrained wp-container-core-group-is-layout-633910b2 wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained\" style=\"padding-top:4.5rem;padding-right:2.5rem;padding-bottom:4.5rem;padding-left:2.5rem\">\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Educating Tenants and Setting Expectations<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Many thermostat conflicts stem from fundamental misunderstandings about how heating systems work and what represents reasonable comfort in older housing stock. Students arriving from newer suburban homes with efficient equipment expect instant warmth and rock-steady temperatures in 1980s duplex construction that cannot deliver that performance.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Landlords who include basic HVAC education in lease signing conversations\u2014explaining system capabilities, realistic temperature expectations, and cost implications of different thermostat strategies\u2014prevent many problems before they develop. A five-minute conversation about why setting the thermostat to eighty-five does not make the house warm up faster and how setback temperatures save money returns value all winter long.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Written guidance provided at move-in reinforces verbal explanations and gives tenants a reference when questions arise mid-semester. A single-page document explaining the specific heating system in the unit, recommended temperature settings, what to do if rooms feel unevenly heated, and when to contact the landlord versus when to adjust settings builds tenant competence.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Including utility cost examples\u2014showing that a five-degree setback overnight saves approximately fifteen percent on heating costs\u2014helps tenants make informed decisions about comfort-versus-cost tradeoffs. Long-term success in student rental properties requires selecting tenants who demonstrate capacity for basic household management and excluding those who view landlords as hospitality providers.<\/p>\n\n<\/div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group has-global-padding is-layout-constrained wp-container-core-group-is-layout-633910b2 wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained\" style=\"padding-top:4.5rem;padding-right:2.5rem;padding-bottom:4.5rem;padding-left:2.5rem\">\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group s-diagnostic has-global-padding is-layout-constrained wp-container-core-group-is-layout-b267b866 wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained\" style=\"padding-top:3rem;padding-right:3rem;padding-bottom:3rem;padding-left:3rem\">\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Landlord Pre-Lease HVAC Checklist<\/h3>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Filter replaced and date written on frame\u2014prevents tenant-caused airflow restriction<\/li>\n\n\n<li>Thermostat lockout set to prevent below-60\u00b0F operation\u2014pipe-freeze protection<\/li>\n\n\n<li>Condensate drain clear and tested\u2014prevents ceiling damage in unit below<\/li>\n\n\n<li>CO detector within 15 feet of all sleeping areas\u2014tested and dated<\/li>\n\n\n<li>Emergency shutoff labeled and accessible\u2014tenant can act before damage compounds<\/li>\n\n\n<li>Ductwork insulated in unconditioned spaces\u2014reduces loss in basement or attic<\/li>\n\n\n<li>Register positions verified\u2014no blocked vents reducing airflow to occupied rooms<\/li>\n\n<\/ul>\n<\/div>\n\n<\/div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group alignfull s-band s-band--ink has-contrast-background-color has-background has-global-padding is-layout-constrained wp-container-core-group-is-layout-08713647 wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained\" style=\"padding-top:6rem;padding-right:2.5rem;padding-bottom:6rem;padding-left:2.5rem\">\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group has-global-padding is-layout-constrained wp-container-core-group-is-layout-633910b2 wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained\" style=\"padding-top:4.5rem;padding-right:2.5rem;padding-bottom:4.5rem;padding-left:2.5rem\">\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group s-quote s-quote--card has-global-padding is-layout-constrained wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained\">\n<figure class=\"wp-block-pullquote\"><blockquote><p>The properties with the fewest HVAC problems are those where landlords invest time in tenant selection and education rather than hoping better equipment will compensate for dysfunction in the relationship.<\/p><cite>Keystone Service, Shippensburg rental housing analysis<\/cite><\/blockquote><\/figure>\n<\/div>\n\n<\/div>\n\n<\/div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group has-global-padding is-layout-constrained wp-container-core-group-is-layout-633910b2 wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained\" style=\"padding-top:4.5rem;padding-right:2.5rem;padding-bottom:4.5rem;padding-left:2.5rem\">\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-element-heading has-text-align-center wp-block-heading\">Questions About HVAC in Shippensburg Rental Properties<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group s-accordion s-accordion--minimal has-global-padding is-layout-constrained wp-container-core-group-is-layout-1583283a wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained\">\n<details class=\"wp-block-details is-layout-flow wp-block-details-is-layout-flow\"><summary>Can my landlord lock me out of the thermostat or limit what temperature I can set?<\/summary>\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Pennsylvania rental law requires landlords to maintain habitable temperatures but does not guarantee tenant control over thermostats. If utilities are included in rent, landlords can implement reasonable restrictions including lockbox covers or smart thermostats with limited adjustment ranges. If you pay utilities separately, restrictions are harder to justify legally. Review your lease for specific language addressing this.<\/p>\n\n<\/details>\n\n\n\n<details class=\"wp-block-details is-layout-flow wp-block-details-is-layout-flow\"><summary>The upstairs stays warm but the downstairs is freezing\u2014whose problem is this?<\/summary>\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Uneven heating in multi-level duplexes typically reflects either undersized ductwork to lower levels, closed or blocked registers, or duct leakage in unconditioned spaces. If you rent the affected area, this is a landlord maintenance responsibility under habitability requirements. Document the temperature differential with photos of thermometers in different areas and submit a written maintenance request requiring response.<\/p>\n\n<\/details>\n\n\n\n<details class=\"wp-block-details is-layout-flow wp-block-details-is-layout-flow\"><summary>Can I install my own smart thermostat if the landlord will not provide one?<\/summary>\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Lease terms typically prohibit modifications to mechanical systems without written permission. Request permission in writing, offering to reinstall the original thermostat when you move out and noting that the upgrade may reduce landlord utility costs if they cover heating. Many landlords approve when framed as a tenant-funded improvement rather than a demand.<\/p>\n\n<\/details>\n\n\n\n<details class=\"wp-block-details is-layout-flow wp-block-details-is-layout-flow\"><summary>What is a normal heating bill for a Shippensburg rental duplex during winter?<\/summary>\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Natural gas heating costs for a 1,200-square-foot unit in poorly insulated rental duplexes typically run $150\u2013$250 per month October through April. Units with R-49 attic insulation, sealed air leaks, and modern furnaces run $80\u2013$130 in the same period. Smart thermostat use and awareness of seasonal settings can reduce bills by 15\u201330% regardless of building condition.<\/p>\n\n<\/details>\n\n\n<\/div>\n\n<\/div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group has-global-padding is-layout-constrained wp-container-core-group-is-layout-633910b2 wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained\" style=\"padding-top:4.5rem;padding-right:2.5rem;padding-bottom:4.5rem;padding-left:2.5rem\">\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group s-nearby has-global-padding is-layout-constrained wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained\">\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><strong>Also serving nearby:<\/strong> <a href=\"\/what-a-maintenance-plan-actually-buys-you-in-chambersburg\/\">Chambersburg<\/a> \u00b7 <a href=\"\/one-thermostat-cant-run-a-three-story-carlisle-foursquare\/\">Carlisle<\/a><\/p>\n<\/div>\n\n<\/div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group has-global-padding is-layout-constrained wp-container-core-group-is-layout-633910b2 wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained\" style=\"padding-top:4.5rem;padding-right:2.5rem;padding-bottom:4.5rem;padding-left:2.5rem\">\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-element-heading has-text-align-center wp-block-heading\">Our Work in Your Neighborhood<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-gallery alignwide has-nested-images columns-3 is-cropped s-gallery wp-block-gallery-1 is-layout-flex wp-block-gallery-is-layout-flex\">\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"1024\" height=\"683\" data-id=\"1476\" src=\"\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez-technician-2-1024x683.png\" alt=\"technician - professional HVAC service photo\" class=\"wp-image-1476\" srcset=\"http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez-technician-2-1024x683.png 1024w, http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez-technician-2-300x200.png 300w, http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez-technician-2-768x512.png 768w, http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez-technician-2.png 1536w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px\" \/><span class=\"s-img-badge s-img-badge--ai\" title=\"AI-generated (gpt-image-1)\">AI<\/span><\/figure>\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"1024\" height=\"674\" data-id=\"175\" src=\"\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/9233808413_0bd6568b24_b.jpg\" alt=\"small town main street pennsylvania\" class=\"wp-image-175\" srcset=\"http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/9233808413_0bd6568b24_b.jpg 1024w, http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/9233808413_0bd6568b24_b-300x197.jpg 300w, http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/9233808413_0bd6568b24_b-768x506.jpg 768w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px\" \/><span class=\"s-img-badge s-img-badge--stock\" title=\"&quot;&#039;Hallowed Ground&#039; -- Gettysburg 150 Years Later July 2013&quot; by Ron Cogswell, BY, via Openverse\">Stock<\/span><\/figure>\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"1024\" height=\"683\" data-id=\"186\" src=\"\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/300873227_7224777c44_b.jpg\" alt=\"boiler pipes heating system\" class=\"wp-image-186\" srcset=\"http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/300873227_7224777c44_b.jpg 1024w, http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/300873227_7224777c44_b-300x200.jpg 300w, http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/300873227_7224777c44_b-768x512.jpg 768w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px\" \/><span class=\"s-img-badge s-img-badge--stock\" title=\"&quot;Pipes&quot; by twoshortplanks, BY-SA, via Openverse\">Stock<\/span><\/figure>\n\n<\/figure>\n\n<\/div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group alignfull s-band s-band--dark-gradient s-band--spacious has-contrast-background-color has-background has-global-padding is-layout-constrained wp-container-core-group-is-layout-08713647 wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained\" style=\"padding-top:6rem;padding-right:2.5rem;padding-bottom:6rem;padding-left:2.5rem\">\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group s-cta--fullbleed has-global-padding is-layout-constrained wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained\">\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">HVAC Solutions for Shippensburg&#039;s Rental Housing Challenges<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Keystone works with property owners and tenants throughout the student housing market to implement smart controls, zoning solutions, and system upgrades that reduce conflict and improve comfort. Whether you manage multiple rental properties or rent a duplex unit where temperature disputes are disrupting your semester, practical solutions exist.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-buttons is-content-justification-center is-layout-flex wp-container-core-buttons-is-layout-35f06ea7 wp-block-buttons-is-layout-flex\">\n<div class=\"wp-block-button\"><a class=\"wp-block-button__link wp-element-button\" href=\"\/contact\/\">Book the Rental Property Audit<\/a><\/div>\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-button is-style-outline is-style-outline--2\"><a class=\"wp-block-button__link wp-element-button\" href=\"tel:+1\">Call Now<\/a><\/div>\n<\/div>\n<\/div>\n\n<\/div>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"s-credits has-small-font-size wp-block-paragraph\">Photos: AI-generated (gemini-2.5-flash-image) \u00b7 &quot;The R11 attic insulation&quot; by zieak, BY, via Openverse<\/p>\n","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"<p>Shippensburg college rental duplexes create unique HVAC thermostat conflicts. Smart controls and zoning solutions for landlords and tenants.<\/p>\n","protected":false},"author":0,"featured_media":1797,"parent":0,"menu_order":0,"comment_status":"closed","ping_status":"closed","template":"location","meta":{"_acf_changed":false,"_angie_page":false,"footnotes":""},"class_list":["post-159","page","type-page","status-publish","has-post-thumbnail","hentry"],"acf":[],"yoast_head":"<!-- This site is optimized with the Yoast SEO plugin v28.0 - https:\/\/yoast.com\/product\/yoast-seo-wordpress\/ -->\n<title>The Thermostat War in Shippensburg Duplexes Has No Winner - Keystone Comfort Co.<\/title>\n<meta name=\"description\" content=\"Shippensburg college rental duplexes create unique HVAC thermostat conflicts. Sm